  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-28T00:09:22.458Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new Dynamic Bone Limiter doesn't seem to be calculating \"Max Affected Transforms\" correctly (and possibly Max Collision Checks), using the latest version: VRChat 2019.1.4p1, build 737.\nI have an avatar that is ranked as Medium with 32 Dynamic Bone Transforms and 8 Dynamic Bone Collision Checks, but all dynamic bone components get disabled as soon as I turn on the limiter with default settings (32 transforms, 8 collision checks).\n\nHere is a video demonstrating this:\nhttps://streamable.com/mvnx8\n\nThrough trial and error via editing the config.json settings file, I found out that they stay enabled when I set the \"Max Affected Transforms\" for the Dynamic Bone Limiter to 45. They stay disabled at 44.\n\nThe avatar does not have any animations or gestures that toggle dynamic bones; it's just a bare-bones avatar with dynamic bones that I uploaded to rule out if anything else was interfering with it.",
